! Xresources — X11 font rendering and scaling. Symlinked to ~/.Xresources and
! merged by i3 on login (exec_always xrdb -merge).
!
! Xft.dpi is how X11 apps get scaled. GNOME did this with
! text-scaling-factor, which i3 does not read.
!
! 110 rather than the default 96 is a touch over 1.15x — enough to make a
! 2560x1600 16-inch panel comfortable without the blurry half-scaling you get from
! jumping to 144. Raise it if you want more; it only ever affects apps started
! afterwards, so reload i3 and reopen them.
Xft.dpi:        110
Xft.antialias:  true
Xft.hinting:    true
Xft.rgba:       rgb
Xft.hintstyle:  hintslight
